body { font-family: sans-serif; }
.list { list-style: none; padding: 0; width: 200px; }
.list li { padding: 8px; }
.list li:nth-child(odd)  { background: #e0f2fe; }
.list li:nth-child(even) { background: #fff; }
.list li:first-child { font-weight: bold; }
.list li:last-child { border-bottom: 3px solid #2965f1; }
.btn { padding: 10px 20px; border: 2px solid #2965f1; background: #fff; border-radius: 6px; }
.btn:hover { background: #2965f1; color: #fff; }
.btn:active { transform: scale(.96); }
.btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid orange; outline-offset: 3px; }

.box { font-family: sans-serif; }
p:first-child { color: red; }      /* no match: h4 is first child */
p:first-of-type { color: green; }  /* matches the first p */

body { font-family: sans-serif; }
input { width: 20px; height: 20px; vertical-align: middle; }
label { padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; margin-left: 6px; background: #e2e8f0; }
input:checked + label { background: #16a34a; color: #fff; }

body { font-family: sans-serif; background: #080a0c; color: azure; padding: 20px; }
.title { position: relative; display: inline-block; font-size: 40px; margin-top: 20px; }
.title::before { content: "THAPA TECHNICAL"; position: absolute; top: -18px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 6px; color: rgb(255,204,112); }
.title::after { content: ""; position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: 2px; width: 60%; border: 2px solid #ae445a; }
.intro::first-letter { font-size: 48px; color: #ae445a; font-weight: bold; }
.intro::first-line { text-decoration: underline; }
.intro::selection { background: rgb(255,204,112); color: #000; }

.ul { position: relative; font: 22px sans-serif; text-decoration: none; color: #0f172a; }
.ul::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: -4px; width: 0; height: 3px; background: #2965f1; transition: width .3s; }
.ul:hover::after { width: 100%; }

topics.description:
Modern CSS added **functional pseudo-classes** that take a selector list. They make code shorter and more powerful.

### :is()
Matches any selector in the list; specificity = the most specific argument.

```css
/* before */
.about h1, .about p, .testimonial h1, .testimonial p { color: yellow; }
/* after */
:is(.about, .testimonial) :is(h1, p) { color: yellow; }
```

### :where()
Same as `:is()` but specificity is **always 0**. Perfect for resets and library defaults that must be easy to override:

```css
:where(h1, h2, h3) { margin-block: 0.5em; }
```

### :not()
Excludes matching elements: `li:not(:last-child) { border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }` or `nav ul :not(li:first-child)` (source demo).

### :has() - the parent selector
Selects an element **based on its descendants or following siblings**:

```css
.card:has(img) { grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; }
.parent:has(input[type="checkbox"]:checked) label { color: red; }
form:has(:invalid) button { opacity: .5; }
label:has(+ input:required)::after { content: " *"; }
```

### :focus-visible and :focus-within
- `:focus-visible` - show rings for keyboard focus only.
- `:focus-within` - parent reacts when any child is focused (highlight a whole form row).

### Browser support
All of these are supported in current evergreen browsers (check caniuse for older targets). Selector lists inside `:is()` are **forgiving** (one invalid selector does not kill the rule).

examples.css:
body { font-family: sans-serif; }
input[type="checkbox"] { accent-color: pink; width: 22px; height: 22px; }
.parent:has(input:checked) label { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.card { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 8px; margin-top: 10px; }
.card:has(img) { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; background: #eef2ff; }

.nav { display: flex; list-style: none; padding: 0; font-family: sans-serif; }
.nav li { padding: 6px 14px; }
:is(.nav) li:not(:last-child) { border-right: 2px solid #94a3b8; }
.nav li:is(:hover, :focus-visible) { background: #2965f1; color: #fff; }

body { font-family: sans-serif; padding: 16px; }
.card {
  width: 280px; padding: 16px; border: 2px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; background: #fff;
  transition: box-shadow .2s, transform .2s;
  & h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: #0f172a; }
  & p { color: #475569; }
  & button { padding: 8px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; background: #2965f1; color: #fff;
    &:hover { background: #1d4ed8; } }
  &:hover { box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.15); transform: translateY(-3px); }
  &.featured { border-color: gold; }
}
